        <mxCell id="how-title" value="How it works" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontStyle=1;fontSize=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="34" y="1452" width="90" height="14" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="how-lines" value="1. Battery (48 V) feeds the terminal block. Motor controller draws BAT+ and GND; outputs 3 phases (U, V, W) to the motor via the same terminal block.&lt;br&gt;2. Buck regulator steps 48 V down to 12 V, distributed through WAGO connectors.&lt;br&gt;3. The 12 V rail feeds the Shutdown Circuit (SDC): a series chain of kill switches, impact switch, and RES (with manual bypass).&lt;br&gt;4. SDC current flows through the relay coil (pin 86 → 85), then to ground via kart_medulla&#39;s N-channel MOSFET.&lt;br&gt;5. When the relay is energized, its N.O. contacts (30 → 87) close, completing the motor controller&#39;s KEY circuit and enabling drive.&lt;br&gt;6. Any open switch in the SDC chain de-energizes the relay → contacts open → motor controller disabled.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Signal &amp;amp; control:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;7. Pedal sensors (linear Hall, 0–5 V) always feed analog signals to kart_medulla for data logging and/or autonomous control.&lt;br&gt;8. SPDT mode switch on the dashboard selects throttle source: manual (pedal → motor ctrl directly) or autonomous (ESP32 DAC → motor ctrl).&lt;br&gt;9. Steering: ESP32 PID reads AS5600 angle sensor (I2C) and drives Cytron MD25HV H-bridge (PWM + DIR) to control the steering motor.&lt;br&gt;10. Brake pedal signal is read by kart_medulla; its DAC output (CMD_BRK) feeds the motor controller&#39;s brake input.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Computer &amp;amp; perception:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;11. Orin (NVIDIA Jetson AGX Orin Developer Kit) connects to kart_medulla via USB-C, to ZED2 camera via USB-A, and draws 12 V via barrel jack." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="34" y="1468" width="1184" height="192" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
